  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "As your Command phase begins, every friendly **ADEPTUS CUSTODES** unit with this ability becomes readied. A readied unit may use any single ka’tah ability from this list, at the moment that ability names; once it does, its readied status ends.\nDacatarai: as any Fight phase begins, pick one readied unit of yours. For the rest of that phase, its melee attacks against an enemy unit that is not a MONSTER or VEHICLE may re-roll a hit roll of 1.\nKaptaris: as any Fight phase begins, pick one readied unit of yours. For the rest of that phase, melee attacks aimed at it suffer −1 to their hit rolls.\nRendax: in any Fight phase, as a readied unit of yours is picked to fight, it can use this; for the rest of that phase its melee attacks gain **[[LETHAL HITS: MONSTER/VEHICLE]](vsdata:weapon-ability/lethal-hits)**.\nConversai: in your Command phase, pick one readied unit of yours. For the rest of that turn, it may still start an action while engaged or battle-shocked, and it may still shoot after it has started an action.\nCalistus: in your Movement phase, as a readied unit of yours is picked to move, it can use this; for the rest of that phase, whenever it makes a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move, it may pass through models of every type.\nSalvus: in your Shooting phase, as a readied unit of yours is picked to shoot, it can use this; for the rest of that phase it may disregard modifiers to its BS and to its hit and wound rolls.\nFavoured Ka’tah: every detachment tagged ‘Unique: Shield Host’ names one ka’tah ability as its Favoured Ka’tah; when you have chosen such a detachment, that ability also gains the extra effect the detachment lists whenever a unit uses it (for example, a unit using Calistus with Solar Watch also gets +2\" Move).",
